  "id": "COMPOUND:25698 - PROTEIN:5807",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a complex but coherent relationship between 3-Methylundecane and prostate cells, mediated through SNU-387 and a series of target molecules. 3-Methylundecane is directly linked to SNU-387, which in turn is a target of multiple compounds, including Quercetagetin 3-methyl ether 7-glucoside and a complex polyketide. These compounds are ultimately shown to have a target on prostate cells, indicating a potential pathway where 3-Methylundecane may influence prostate cell function through these intermediates. The evidence supports a mechanism where 3-Methylundecane could act as a modulator or activator of the target pathways, possibly through interaction with the polyketide compounds or their downstream effects on prostate cells. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible role for 3-Methylundecane in the regulation of prostate cell activity, though the exact mechanism remains to be elucidated.",
